/-!
# Uniform vanishing of Tor transition maps for modules of bounded torsion

Let `I` be an ideal in a Noetherian ring. In each positive degree, and for each fixed power
`I ^ m`, there is a uniform shift after which the transition maps between the Tor modules of the
quotients by powers of `I` vanish for every module annihilated by `I ^ m`.

When `I` is generated by at most `t` elements, the restriction to modules of bounded torsion can
be removed in degree `t + 1`: there are a threshold `N` and a shift `c`, depending only on `A`,
`I` and `t`, such that the transition on `Tor_{t+1}` vanishes for *every* `A`-module and every
`n ≥ N`.

## Main results

* `exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_smul_eq_bot` gives the uniform shift for all
  modules annihilated by a fixed power of the ideal.
* `exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator` gives the uniform shift in
  degree `t + 1` for all modules at once, from the uniform annihilation of
  [Stacks, Tag 0GA1].
* `exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_tor'`: **[Stacks, Tag 0GA2]**,
  the uniform vanishing of the transition on `Tor_{t+1}` for every module, for an ideal generated
  by at most `t` elements of a Noetherian ring.
* `exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level` and
  `exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level_tor'` are the same two
  statements with the degree of the conclusion decoupled from the number of generators: if the
  uniform annihilation holds in all degrees above a level `e`, the transition on `Tor_{e+1}`
  vanishes, whatever `e` and `t` are.

## The proof of [Stacks, Tag 0GA2]

The degree `t + 1` statement is deduced, as in the source, from the conclusion of
[Stacks, Tag 0GA1]: a single power `I ^ c₁`, depending on `A` and `I` alone, annihilates
`Tor_i^A(M, A/I^q)` for every module `M`, every `i > t` and every `q`. The deduction is the
descending induction on the number of generators whose `c₁`-st power acts as zero, its base case
from [Stacks, Tag 0G9X], and the diagram chase of the two short exact sequences attached to
multiplication by such a generator; it is carried out for any `c₁` with that property, in
`exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator`. The annihilation itself is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII.exists_pow_le_annihilator_tor_quotient_pow_blowup`, proved on
the blowup of `Spec A` in `I` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.BitUniformityII.TorAnnihilationBlowup`.

## Implementation notes

An `A`-module is annihilated by `I ^ m` when the submodule generated by the action of `I ^ m` is
bottom. The transition between quotient modules is the canonical map induced by the inclusion
`I ^ n ≤ I ^ (n - c)`. The induction on the Tor degree replaces a module of bounded torsion by
the kernel of its canonical presentation by copies of `A / I ^ m`, which again has bounded
torsion; the uniform shift doubles at each step.

An upper bound of `t` on the number of generators of `I` is presented by a generating family
indexed by `Fin t`. In the base case of the descending induction all of `g 0 ^ c₁, …` act as
zero on the module, and the power of `I` that then annihilates it comes from the inclusion of
some power of `I` in the ideal they generate, which holds because `I` is finitely generated and
lies in the radical of that ideal.

The number of generators and the level of the annihilation hypothesis enter the induction
separately: the generators index its steps, each costing one degree of headroom above the level,
while the level alone fixes the degree of the conclusion.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G9X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G9X)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GA2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA2)
-/

@[expose] public section


open CategoryTheory
open CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

/-- For a finite module the uniform shift comes directly from pro-vanishing of Tor. -/
private theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_finite
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) [Module.Finite A M] (i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ n : ℕ, c ≤ n →
      ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨c, _, hc⟩ := tor_pro_zero (A := A) I M hi
  refine ⟨c, fun n hn ↦ ?_⟩
  show ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map
    (torProZeroTransition I (Nat.sub_le n c)) = 0
  exact hc n hn

/-- Tensoring with a complex is additive. -/
private instance torTensorComplex_additive
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (Pc : ChainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℕ) : (torTensorComplex Pc).Additive where
  map_add {X Y f g} := HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun k ↦
    ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.rTensor_add (Pc.X k) f.hom g.hom)

/-- `Tor` is additive in its second variable. -/
private noncomputable instance torFlip_additive
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i : ℕ) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.obj N).Additive := by
  let P := projectiveResolution N
  let F := torTensorComplex P.complex
  let H := HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor
    (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.down ℕ) i
  let e := torFlipObjIsoTensorComplexHomology N i P
  have : F.Additive := torTensorComplex_additive P.complex
  exact (Functor.additive_iff_of_iso e).2 inferInstance

/-- A natural transformation vanishing on the pieces of a colimit preserved by its source
vanishes on every object isomorphic to the colimit point. -/
private theorem natTrans_app_eq_zero_of_isColimit
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {J : Type*} [Category J]
    {F F' : ModuleCat.{u} A ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A} (η : F ⟶ F') {D : J ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A}
    {C : Cocone D} (hFC : IsColimit (F.mapCocone C)) (hD : ∀ j, η.app (D.obj j) = 0)
    {X : ModuleCat.{u} A} (e : X ≅ C.pt) : η.app X = 0 := by
  have hpt : η.app C.pt = 0 := by
    refine hFC.hom_ext fun j ↦ ?_
    rw [Functor.mapCocone_ι_app, η.naturality, hD j, Limits.zero_comp, Limits.comp_zero]
  refine (cancel_mono (F'.map e.hom)).mp ?_
  rw [Limits.zero_comp, ← η.naturality e.hom, hpt, Limits.comp_zero]

/-- Vanishing of a Tor transition map passes to a finite direct sum of copies. -/
private theorem tor_transition_zero_finsupp_finite
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} [Finite ι]
    (i : ℕ) (Q N N' : ModuleCat.{u} A) (g : N ⟶ N')
    (hQ : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj Q).map g = 0) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj (ModuleCat.of A (ι →₀ Q))).map g = 0 := by
  classical
  let F := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.obj N
  let F' := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.obj N'
  let η := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.map g
  let Z : ι → ModuleCat.{u} A := fun _ ↦ Q
  let C := colimit.cocone (Discrete.functor Z)
  have hC : IsColimit C := colimit.isColimit (Discrete.functor Z)
  have : F.Additive := torFlip_additive N i
  have hFC : IsColimit (F.mapCocone C) := isColimitOfPreserves F hC
  let e : ModuleCat.of A (ι →₀ Q) ≅ C.pt :=
    (finsuppLEquivDirectSum A Q ι).toModuleIso ≪≫
      (ModuleCat.coprodIsoDirectSum Z).symm
  exact natTrans_app_eq_zero_of_isColimit η hFC (fun j ↦ by simpa [η, Z] using hQ) e

/-- The summand of a free module supported on a finite subset of the index type. -/
private abbrev finiteSupportSum
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} (Q : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (s : Finset ι) := (↑s →₀ Q)

/-- The inclusion of one finite-support summand into a larger one. -/
private noncomputable def finiteSupportSumMap
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} (Q : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    {s t : Finset ι} (h : s ⊆ t) :
    finiteSupportSum Q s →ₗ[A] finiteSupportSum Q t :=
  Finsupp.lmapDomain (↑Q) A (α' := ↑t) (fun x : ↑s ↦ ⟨x.1, h x.2⟩)

/-- The inclusion of a finite-support summand into the whole free module. -/
private noncomputable def finiteSupportSumInto
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} (Q : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (s : Finset ι) : finiteSupportSum Q s →ₗ[A] (ι →₀ Q) :=
  Finsupp.lmapDomain (↑Q) A (α' := ι) (fun x : ↑s ↦ x.1)

/-- The finite-support summands form a directed system. -/
private theorem finiteSupportSum_system
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} (Q : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    DirectedSystem (fun s : Finset ι ↦ finiteSupportSum Q s)
      (fun _ _ h ↦ finiteSupportSumMap Q h) where
  map_self := by
    intro s x
    ext a
    simp [finiteSupportSumMap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply]
  map_map := by
    intro i j k hij hjk x
    ext a
    simp [finiteSupportSumMap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply, ← Finsupp.mapDomain_comp]

/-- The inclusions into the whole free module are compatible with the directed system. -/
private theorem finiteSupportSum_compat
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} (Q : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
    ∀ (s t : Finset ι) (h : s ≤ t) (x : finiteSupportSum Q s),
      finiteSupportSumInto Q t (finiteSupportSumMap Q h x) =
        finiteSupportSumInto Q s x := by
  intro s t h x
  ext a
  simp [finiteSupportSumInto, finiteSupportSumMap, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply,
    ← Finsupp.mapDomain_comp]

/-- A free module is the direct limit of its finite-support summands. -/
private noncomputable def finiteSupportSum_limitEquiv
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u} (Q : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    [DecidableEq ι] :
    Module.DirectLimit (fun s : Finset ι ↦ finiteSupportSum Q s)
      (fun _ _ h ↦ finiteSupportSumMap Q h) ≃ₗ[A] (ι →₀ Q) := by
  let f : ∀ s t : Finset ι, s ≤ t → finiteSupportSum Q s →ₗ[A] finiteSupportSum Q t :=
    fun s t h ↦ finiteSupportSumMap Q h
  let g : ∀ s : Finset ι, finiteSupportSum Q s →ₗ[A] (ι →₀ Q) :=
    finiteSupportSumInto Q
  let hcompat : ∀ s t (h : s ≤ t) x, g t (f s t h x) = g s x :=
    fun s t h x ↦ finiteSupportSum_compat Q s t h x
  let : DirectedSystem (fun s : Finset ι ↦ finiteSupportSum Q s)
      (fun ⦃s t⦄ h ↦ f s t h) := finiteSupportSum_system Q
  let lift := Module.DirectLimit.lift A (Finset ι) _ f g hcompat
  have hinj : Function.Injective lift := Module.DirectLimit.lift_injective g hcompat
    (fun s ↦ by
      intro x y hxy
      ext a
      have hh := congrArg (fun z : ι →₀ Q ↦ z a.1) hxy
      simpa [g, finiteSupportSumInto, Finsupp.lmapDomain_apply,
        Finsupp.mapDomain_apply] using hh)
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective lift := by
    intro z
    let s : Finset ι := z.support
    let e : ↑s ↪ ι := ⟨Subtype.val, Subtype.val_injective⟩
    let x : ↑s →₀ Q := Finsupp.comapDomain e z (by
      intro a ha b hb hab
      exact Subtype.ext hab)
    refine ⟨Module.DirectLimit.of A (Finset ι) _ f s x, ?_⟩
    simp only [lift, Module.DirectLimit.lift_of]
    change Finsupp.mapDomain Subtype.val x = z
    calc
      _ = Finsupp.embDomain e x := (Finsupp.embDomain_eq_mapDomain e x).symm
      _ = z := Finsupp.embDomain_comapDomain (by
        intro y hy
        exact ⟨⟨y, by simpa [s] using hy⟩, rfl⟩)
  simpa [f] using LinearEquiv.ofBijective lift ⟨hinj, hsurj⟩

/-- Vanishing of a Tor transition map passes to an arbitrary direct sum of copies. -/
private theorem tor_transition_zero_finsupp
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type u}
    (i : ℕ) (Q N N' : ModuleCat.{u} A) (g : N ⟶ N')
    (hQ : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj Q).map g = 0) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj (ModuleCat.of A (ι →₀ Q))).map g = 0 := by
  classical
  let G : Finset ι → Type u := fun s ↦ finiteSupportSum Q s
  let f : ∀ s t : Finset ι, s ≤ t → G s →ₗ[A] G t :=
    fun s t h ↦ finiteSupportSumMap Q h
  let : DirectedSystem G (fun s t h ↦ f s t h) := finiteSupportSum_system Q
  let C := ModuleCat.directLimitCocone G f
  have hC : IsColimit C := ModuleCat.directLimitIsColimit G f
  let F := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.obj N
  let F' := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.obj N'
  let η := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.map g
  have hpres : PreservesColimit (ModuleCat.directLimitDiagram G f) F :=
    tor_flip_preservesColimit_directLimit G f N i
  have hFC : IsColimit (F.mapCocone C) := isColimitOfPreserves F hC
  let e : ModuleCat.of A (ι →₀ Q) ≅ C.pt :=
    (finiteSupportSum_limitEquiv Q).symm.toModuleIso
  exact natTrans_app_eq_zero_of_isColimit η hFC
    (fun s ↦ tor_transition_zero_finsupp_finite i Q N N' g hQ) e

/-- An ideal annihilates a module iff its elements act as zero on every element. -/
private theorem ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] (J : Ideal A) :
    J • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥ ↔ ∀ a ∈ J, ∀ x : M, a • x = 0 := by
  rw [← Submodule.le_annihilator_iff, Submodule.annihilator_top]
  simp [SetLike.le_def, Module.mem_annihilator]

/-- Multiplication by a module element, as a map out of the ring. -/
private noncomputable def boundedTorsionCyclicMap
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (x : (M : Type u)) :
    A →ₗ[A] (M : Type u) where
  toFun r := r • x
  map_add' r s := add_smul r s x
  map_smul' r s := mul_smul r s x

/-- If `I ^ m` annihilates `M`, it is contained in the kernel of multiplication by any element
of `M`. -/
private theorem boundedTorsionPow_le_ker_cyclicMap
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m : ℕ)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (hM : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥)
    (x : (M : Type u)) : I ^ m ≤ LinearMap.ker (boundedTorsionCyclicMap M x) := by
  intro r hr
  exact LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr ((ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff _).mp hM r hr x)

/-- Multiplication by an element of a module annihilated by `I ^ m`, as a map out of
`A / I ^ m`. -/
private noncomputable def boundedTorsionQuotientMap
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m : ℕ)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (hM : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥) (x : M) :
    (A ⧸ I ^ m) →ₗ[A] M :=
  Submodule.liftQ (I ^ m) (boundedTorsionCyclicMap M x)
    (boundedTorsionPow_le_ker_cyclicMap I m M hM x)

/-- The canonical presentation of a module annihilated by `I ^ m` by copies of `A / I ^ m`. -/
private noncomputable def boundedTorsionPresentationMap
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m : ℕ)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (hM : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥) :
    (M →₀ A ⧸ I ^ m) →ₗ[A] M := by
  classical
  exact (DirectSum.toModule A M M (boundedTorsionQuotientMap I m M hM)).comp
    (finsuppLEquivDirectSum A (A ⧸ I ^ m) M).toLinearMap

/-- The canonical presentation is surjective. -/
private theorem boundedTorsionPresentationMap_surjective
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m : ℕ)
    (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (hM : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥) :
    Function.Surjective (boundedTorsionPresentationMap I m M hM) := by
  classical
  intro x
  refine ⟨Finsupp.single x (Submodule.Quotient.mk (1 : A)), ?_⟩
  show DirectSum.toModule A M M (boundedTorsionQuotientMap I m M hM)
    (finsuppLEquivDirectSum A (A ⧸ I ^ m) M
      (Finsupp.single x (Submodule.Quotient.mk (1 : A)))) = x
  rw [finsuppLEquivDirectSum_single, DirectSum.toModule_lof]
  show (Submodule.liftQ (I ^ m) (boundedTorsionCyclicMap M x)
    (boundedTorsionPow_le_ker_cyclicMap I m M hM x))
      (Submodule.Quotient.mk (1 : A)) = x
  rw [Submodule.liftQ_apply]
  simp [boundedTorsionCyclicMap]

/-- A direct sum of copies of `A / I ^ m` is annihilated by `I ^ m`. -/
private theorem pow_smul_finsupp_eq_bot
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m : ℕ) {ι : Type u} :
    I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A (ι →₀ A ⧸ I ^ m)) = ⊥ := by
  classical
  refine (ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff _).mpr fun a ha x ↦ ?_
  ext j
  have hq : (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ m) a : A ⧸ I ^ m) = 0 :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr ha
  show (Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ m) a) * x j = 0
  rw [hq, zero_mul]

/-- A submodule of a module annihilated by `I ^ m` is annihilated by `I ^ m`. -/
private theorem pow_smul_ker_eq_bot
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m : ℕ)
    {F M : ModuleCat.{u} A} (f : F ⟶ M)
    (hF : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A F) = ⊥) :
    I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A (LinearMap.ker f.hom)) = ⊥ := by
  refine (ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff _).mpr fun a ha x ↦ ?_
  exact Subtype.ext ((ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff _).mp hF a ha (x : F))

/-- Naturality of the comparison between homology of a mapped projective resolution and the
left derived functor, in the natural-transformation variable. -/
private theorem torMapHomologyComm
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {F G : ModuleCat.{u} A ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A}
    [F.Additive] [G.Additive] (α : F ⟶ G) {N : ModuleCat.{u} A}
    (P : ProjectiveResolution N) (i : ℕ) :
    (NatTrans.leftDerived α i).app N ≫ (P.isoLeftDerivedObj G i).hom =
      (P.isoLeftDerivedObj F i).hom ≫
        HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
          ((NatTrans.mapHomologicalComplex α (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).app P.complex) i := by
  rw [P.leftDerived_app_eq α i]
  -- `simp` cannot re-associate or cancel here: the goal is not type-correct at `instances`
  -- transparency. Associativity is `rfl` in `ModuleCat`, so the cancellation is done as a term.
  exact congrArg (fun k ↦ (P.isoLeftDerivedObj F i).hom ≫ k)
    ((congrArg (fun z ↦ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
        ((NatTrans.mapHomologicalComplex α (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).app P.complex) i ≫ z)
      (P.isoLeftDerivedObj G i).inv_hom_id).trans (Category.comp_id _))

/-- The specialization of `torMapHomologyComm` to the tensoring functors computing `Tor`. -/
private theorem torMapHomologyCommTor
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {X Y : ModuleCat.{u} A} (f : X ⟶ Y)
    (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (P : ProjectiveResolution N) (i : ℕ) :
    (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map f).app N) ≫
        (P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj Y) i).hom =
      (P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj X) i).hom ≫
        HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
          ((NatTrans.mapHomologicalComplex
            ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map f) (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).app P.complex) i :=
  torMapHomologyComm ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map f) P i

/-- The connecting map `Tor_i(X₃, N) ⟶ Tor_{i-1}(X₁, N)` of a short exact sequence. -/
private noncomputable def torSESDelta
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)}
    (N : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (hV : (S.map (lesShift.phi A (projectiveResolution N).complex)).ShortExact)
    (i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj S.X₃).obj N) ⟶
      (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj S.X₁).obj N) := by
  let P := projectiveResolution N
  have hrel : (ComplexShape.down ℕ).Rel i (i - 1) := by
    simp only [ComplexShape.down_Rel]
    omega
  exact (P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃) i).hom ≫
    hV.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫
    (P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁) (i - 1)).inv

/-- `torSESDelta` is natural in the second variable. -/
private theorem torSESDelta_naturality_in_second
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)}
    (hS : S.ShortExact) {N N' : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : N ⟶ N')
    (i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj S.X₃).map g) ≫
        torSESDelta N' (lesShift.ses A S hS N') i hi =
      torSESDelta N (lesShift.ses A S hS N) i hi ≫
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj S.X₁).map g) := by
  let P := projectiveResolution N
  let P' := projectiveResolution N'
  let φ := ProjectiveResolution.lift g P P'
  have hφ : φ.f 0 ≫ P'.π.f 0 = P.π.f 0 ≫ g :=
    ProjectiveResolution.lift_commutes_zero g P P'
  let hVN := lesShift.ses A S hS N
  let hVN' := lesShift.ses A S hS N'
  have : ((lesShift.phiBi A).flip.obj P.complex).PreservesZeroMorphisms := by
    show (lesShift.phi A P.complex).PreservesZeroMorphisms
    exact lesShift.phi_preservesZeroMorphisms A P.complex
  have : ((lesShift.phiBi A).flip.obj P'.complex).PreservesZeroMorphisms := by
    show (lesShift.phi A P'.complex).PreservesZeroMorphisms
    exact lesShift.phi_preservesZeroMorphisms A P'.complex
  let ψ := S.mapNatTrans ((lesShift.phiBi A).flip.map φ)
  have hrel : (ComplexShape.down ℕ).Rel i (i - 1) := by
    simp only [ComplexShape.down_Rel]
    omega
  let e₃ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃) i
  let e₃' := P'.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃) i
  let e₁ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁) (i - 1)
  let e₁' := P'.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁) (i - 1)
  have hA : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj S.X₃).map g) ≫ e₃'.hom =
      e₃.hom ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₃ i :=
    ProjectiveResolution.isoLeftDerivedObj_hom_naturality g P P' φ hφ
      (tensorLeft S.X₃) i
  have hC : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj S.X₁).map g) ≫ e₁'.hom =
      e₁.hom ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₁ (i - 1) :=
    ProjectiveResolution.isoLeftDerivedObj_hom_naturality g P P' φ hφ
      (tensorLeft S.X₁) (i - 1)
  have hC' : HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₁ (i - 1) ≫ e₁'.inv =
      e₁.inv ≫ (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj S.X₁).map g) :=
    lesShift.comp_inv_eq_inv_comp_of_comm _ _ _ _ hC
  have hδ := lesShift.δ_naturality A hVN hVN' ψ i (i - 1) hrel
  show (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj S.X₃).map g) ≫ e₃'.hom ≫
      hVN'.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁'.inv =
    e₃.hom ≫ hVN.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁.inv ≫
      (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj S.X₁).map g)
  -- As above, a chain of typed `have`s: each endpoint is written out, so no intermediate
  -- relation is left for `Trans` to guess.
  have s1 : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj S.X₃).map g) ≫ e₃'.hom ≫
        hVN'.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁'.inv =
      e₃.hom ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₃ i ≫
        hVN'.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁'.inv :=
    congrArg (fun k ↦ k ≫ hVN'.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁'.inv) hA
  have s2 : e₃.hom ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₃ i ≫
        hVN'.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁'.inv =
      e₃.hom ≫ hVN.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫
        HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₁ (i - 1) ≫ e₁'.inv :=
    (congrArg (fun k ↦ e₃.hom ≫ k ≫ e₁'.inv) hδ).symm
  have s3 : e₃.hom ≫ hVN.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫
        HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ψ.τ₁ (i - 1) ≫ e₁'.inv =
      e₃.hom ≫ hVN.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ e₁.inv ≫
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj S.X₁).map g) :=
    congrArg (fun k ↦ e₃.hom ≫ hVN.δ i (i - 1) hrel ≫ k) hC'
  exact (s1.trans s2).trans s3

/-- Three consecutive terms of the Tor long exact sequence, as a short complex. -/
private noncomputable def torSESShortComplex
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)}
    (hS : S.ShortExact) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) := by
  let P := projectiveResolution N
  let V := S.map (lesShift.phi A P.complex)
  let hV := lesShift.ses A S hS N
  let η := (NatTrans.mapHomologicalComplex
    ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map S.g) (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).app P.complex
  let ηH := (HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (ComplexShape.down ℕ) i).map η
  have hrel : (ComplexShape.down ℕ).Rel i (i - 1) := by
    simp only [ComplexShape.down_Rel]
    omega
  let e₂ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₂) i
  let e₃ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃) i
  let e₁ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁) (i - 1)
  -- `hV.δ` is typed at `(S.map (lesShift.phi A P.complex)).X₃.homology i`, while everything
  -- else here is typed at `(((tensoringLeft _).obj S.X₃).mapHomologicalComplex _).obj
  -- P.complex |>.homology i`. The two are one object, identified only by unfolding
  -- `lesShift.phi`'s bifunctor, and a goal mixing them is not type-correct at `instances`
  -- transparency, so `simp` refuses to touch it. Ascribing the connecting map once puts the
  -- whole argument into a single vocabulary.
  let δ : ((((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).obj P.complex).homology i ⟶
      ((((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).obj P.complex).homology (i - 1) :=
    hV.δ i (i - 1) hrel
  have hcomm : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N) ≫ e₃.hom =
      e₂.hom ≫ ηH := by
    change (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N) ≫ e₃.hom =
      e₂.hom ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap η i
    exact torMapHomologyCommTor S.g N P i
  refine ShortComplex.mk (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N)
    (torSESDelta N hV i hi) ?_
  have hzero : ηH ≫ δ = 0 := hV.comp_δ i (i - 1) hrel
  change (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N) ≫ e₃.hom ≫ δ ≫ e₁.inv = 0
  have hcomm' := congrArg (fun k ↦ k ≫ δ ≫ e₁.inv) hcomm
  have s1 : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N) ≫ e₃.hom ≫ δ ≫ e₁.inv =
      (e₂.hom ≫ ηH) ≫ δ ≫ e₁.inv := hcomm'
  have s2 : (e₂.hom ≫ ηH) ≫ δ ≫ e₁.inv = e₂.hom ≫ (ηH ≫ δ) ≫ e₁.inv := rfl
  have s3 : e₂.hom ≫ (ηH ≫ δ) ≫ e₁.inv = 0 := by
    rw [hzero]
    exact (congrArg (fun z ↦ e₂.hom ≫ z) Limits.zero_comp).trans Limits.comp_zero
  exact (s1.trans s2).trans s3

/-- The three consecutive terms of the Tor long exact sequence are exact. -/
private theorem torSES_exact
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)}
    (hS : S.ShortExact) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    (torSESShortComplex hS N i hi).Exact := by
  let P := projectiveResolution N
  let V := S.map (lesShift.phi A P.complex)
  let hV := lesShift.ses A S hS N
  let η := (NatTrans.mapHomologicalComplex
    ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map S.g) (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).app P.complex
  let ηH := (HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (ComplexShape.down ℕ) i).map η
  have hrel : (ComplexShape.down ℕ).Rel i (i - 1) := by
    simp only [ComplexShape.down_Rel]
    omega
  let e₂ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₂) i
  let e₃ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃) i
  let e₁ := P.isoLeftDerivedObj ((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁) (i - 1)
  -- `hV.δ` is typed at `(S.map (lesShift.phi A P.complex)).X₃.homology i`, while everything
  -- else here is typed at `(((tensoringLeft _).obj S.X₃).mapHomologicalComplex _).obj
  -- P.complex |>.homology i`. The two are one object, identified only by unfolding
  -- `lesShift.phi`'s bifunctor, and a goal mixing them is not type-correct at `instances`
  -- transparency, so `simp` refuses to touch it. Ascribing the connecting map once puts the
  -- whole argument into a single vocabulary.
  let δ : ((((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₃).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).obj P.complex).homology i ⟶
      ((((tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S.X₁).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.down ℕ)).obj P.complex).homology (i - 1) :=
    hV.δ i (i - 1) hrel
  let H := ShortComplex.mk ηH δ (hV.comp_δ i (i - 1) hrel)
  have hHexact : H.Exact := hV.homology_exact₃ i (i - 1) hrel
  unfold torSESShortComplex
  have hcommg : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N) ≫ e₃.hom =
      e₂.hom ≫ H.f := torMapHomologyCommTor S.g N P i
  have hcommδ : torSESDelta N hV i hi ≫ e₁.hom = e₃.hom ≫ H.g := by
    show e₃.hom ≫ δ ≫ e₁.inv ≫ e₁.hom = e₃.hom ≫ δ
    exact congrArg (fun k ↦ e₃.hom ≫ k)
      ((congrArg (fun z ↦ δ ≫ z) e₁.inv_hom_id).trans (Category.comp_id δ))
  let e : torSESShortComplex hS N i hi ≅ H :=
    ShortComplex.isoMk (S₁ := torSESShortComplex hS N i hi) (S₂ := H)
      e₂ e₃ e₁ hcommg.symm hcommδ.symm
  exact ShortComplex.exact_of_iso e.symm hHexact

/-- The three consecutive terms of the Tor long exact sequence are natural in the second
variable. -/
private noncomputable def torSESShortComplexTransition
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)}
    (hS : S.ShortExact) {N N' : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : N ⟶ N')
    (i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    torSESShortComplex hS N i hi ⟶ torSESShortComplex hS N' i hi := by
  let η := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).flip.map g
  let η' := (Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).flip.map g
  refine ShortComplex.homMk (η.app S.X₂) (η.app S.X₃) (η'.app S.X₁) ?_ ?_
  · change η.app S.X₂ ≫ ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N' =
      ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).map S.g).app N ≫ η.app S.X₃
    exact (η.naturality S.g).symm
  · change η.app S.X₃ ≫ torSESDelta N' (lesShift.ses A S hS N') i hi =
      torSESDelta N (lesShift.ses A S hS N) i hi ≫ η'.app S.X₁
    exact torSESDelta_naturality_in_second hS g i hi

/-- Two consecutive maps of short complexes through an exact one compose to zero on the middle
terms once the outer components vanish. -/
private theorem shortComplex_twoStep_zero
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S T U : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)}
    (hT : T.Exact) (ψ : S ⟶ T) (θ : T ⟶ U)
    (hψ : ψ.τ₃ = 0) (hθ : θ.τ₁ = 0) : ψ.τ₂ ≫ θ.τ₂ = 0 := by
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  apply LinearMap.ext
  intro x
  have hker : T.g.hom (ψ.τ₂.hom x) = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun f ↦ f x) ψ.comm₂₃
    simpa [hψ] using h
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (T.moduleCat_exact_iff.mp hT) (ψ.τ₂.hom x) hker
  have hcomp : U.f.hom (θ.τ₁.hom y) = θ.τ₂.hom (T.f.hom y) := by
    have h := congrArg (fun f ↦ f y) θ.comm₁₂
    simpa using h
  calc
    θ.τ₂.hom (ψ.τ₂.hom x) = θ.τ₂.hom (T.f.hom y) := by rw [← hy]
    _ = U.f.hom (θ.τ₁.hom y) := hcomp.symm
    _ = 0 := by simp [hθ]

/-- The case `i = 1` of the uniform vanishing, by the Artin–Rees lemma. -/
private theorem tor_one_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_smul_eq_bot
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (m n : ℕ)
    (hM : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥) (hmn : m ≤ n) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 1).obj M).map
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - m))
        (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n m)))) = 0 := by
  let π := Projective.π M
  let P := Projective.over M
  let K := LinearMap.ker π.hom
  have hIK : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A P) ≤ K := by
    rw [Submodule.smul_le]
    intro a ha p _
    exact LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr
      (by rw [map_smul]; exact (ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff _).mp hM a ha _)
  have hAR : K ⊓ (I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A P)) ≤ I ^ (n - m) • K := by
    calc
      K ⊓ (I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A P)) ≤ I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule A P) := inf_le_right
      _ = I ^ (n - m) • (I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A P)) := by
        rw [← Submodule.mul_smul, ← pow_add, Nat.sub_add_cancel hmn]
      _ ≤ I ^ (n - m) • K := Submodule.smul_mono le_rfl hIK
  let S := Limits.kernel π
  let α := Tor_iso_Tor'.oneIso_torKer A M
  let η := (MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map
    (Limits.kernel.ι π)
  let F := Limits.kernel η
  let tr := ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - m))
    (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n m)))
  have hF : F.map tr = 0 := by
    have hcomp (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) :
        (PreservesKernel.iso ((evaluation (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj N) η).hom ≫
            Limits.kernel.ι (η.app N) = (Limits.kernel.ι η).app N := by
      rw [PreservesKernel.iso_hom]
      exact kernelComparison_comp_ι η ((evaluation (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj N)
    have hmono : Mono ((Limits.kernel.ι η).app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m)))) := by
      rw [← hcomp]
      infer_instance
    rw [← cancel_mono ((Limits.kernel.ι η).app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m)))),
      Limits.zero_comp]
    show (Limits.kernel η).map tr ≫
      (Limits.kernel.ι η).app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m))) = 0
    rw [(Limits.kernel.ι η).naturality tr]
    rw [← hcomp, Category.assoc]
    suffices hkey : Limits.kernel.ι (η.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n))) ≫
        ((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S).map tr = 0 by
      rw [hkey, Limits.comp_zero]
    let u := η.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n))
    let e := ModuleCat.kernelIsoKer π
    let eT := (MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).mapIso e
    let g := (MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map
      (ModuleCat.ofHom K.subtype)
    have hfactor : eT.hom.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)) ≫
        g.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)) = u := by
      show ((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map e.hom).app _ ≫
          ((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map
            (ModuleCat.ofHom K.subtype)).app _ =
          ((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).map (Limits.kernel.ι π)).app _
      rw [← NatTrans.comp_app, ← Functor.map_comp,
        ModuleCat.kernelIsoKer_hom_ker_subtype]
    rw [← cancel_epi (ModuleCat.kernelIsoKer u).inv, Limits.comp_zero, ← Category.assoc,
      ModuleCat.kernelIsoKer_inv_kernel_ι]
    apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
    apply LinearMap.ext
    rintro ⟨w, hw⟩
    let w' := (eT.hom.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n))).hom w
    have hw' : LinearMap.rTensor (A ⧸ I ^ n) K.subtype w' = 0 := by
      have hh := congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom w) hfactor
      change (g.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n))).hom w' = u.hom w at hh
      change LinearMap.rTensor (A ⧸ I ^ n) K.subtype w' = u.hom w at hh
      have hu : u.hom w = 0 := LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hw
      calc
        _ = u.hom w := hh
        _ = 0 := hu
    have hlin := lTensor_factor_eq_zero_of_rTensor_subtype_eq_zero
      (A := A) I K (Nat.sub_le n m) hAR hw'
    have hnat := (eT.hom).naturality tr
    have hh := congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom w) hnat
    have hleft : (((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of A K)).map tr).hom w' = 0 := hlin
    have hh' : (((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of A K)).map tr).hom w' =
        (eT.hom.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m)))).hom
          ((((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S).map tr).hom w) := by
      simpa [w', ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply] using hh.symm
    have hhzero : (eT.hom.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m)))).hom
        ((((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj S).map tr).hom w) = 0 := by
      calc
        _ = (((MonoidalCategory.tensoringLeft (ModuleCat.{u} A)).obj
          (ModuleCat.of A K)).map tr).hom w' := hh'.symm
        _ = 0 := hleft
    exact ((eT.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m)))).toLinearEquiv.map_eq_zero_iff).mp hhzero
  have hnat := α.hom.naturality tr
  have hnat' : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 1).obj M).map tr ≫
      α.hom.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m))) =
      α.hom.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)) ≫ F.map tr := hnat
  rw [hF] at hnat'
  -- `f ≫ 0 = 0` is `rfl` in `ModuleCat`, so no rewrite is needed on the right of `hnat'`;
  -- `rewrite` could not perform it anyway, the goal not being type-correct at `instances`
  -- transparency.
  refine (Iso.cancel_iso_hom_right _ _ (α.app (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - m))))).mp ?_
  refine hnat'.trans ?_
  exact Limits.comp_zero.trans Limits.zero_comp.symm

/-- Vanishing of a Tor transition map at one shift gives vanishing at every larger target. -/
private theorem tor_transition_zero_to_target
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (i c₀ n m : ℕ) (_hc₀n : c₀ ≤ n) (hm : m ≤ n - c₀)
    (h₀ : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c₀))
        (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c₀)))) = 0) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map
      (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ m)
        (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (hm.trans (Nat.sub_le n c₀))))) = 0 := by
  let q₀ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)
  let q₁ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - c₀))
  let q₂ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ m)
  have h₀₁ : n - c₀ ≤ n := Nat.sub_le n c₀
  have h₀₂ : m ≤ n := hm.trans (Nat.sub_le n c₀)
  let t₀₁ : q₀ ⟶ q₁ := ModuleCat.ofHom
    (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c₀))
      (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁))
  let t₁₂ : q₁ ⟶ q₂ := ModuleCat.ofHom
    (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ (n - c₀)) (p' := I ^ m)
      (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right hm))
  let t₀₂ : q₀ ⟶ q₂ := ModuleCat.ofHom
    (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ m)
      (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₂))
  have hcomp : t₀₁ ≫ t₁₂ = t₀₂ :=
    ModuleCat.hom_ext (Submodule.factor_comp (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁)
      (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right hm))
  calc
    _ = ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map t₀₁ ≫
        ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map t₁₂ := by
          rw [← Functor.map_comp, hcomp]
    _ = 0 := by rw [h₀]; simp

/-- The uniform vanishing, by strong induction on the Tor degree. -/
private theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_core
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m i : ℕ)
    (hi : 0 < i) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A),
      I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥ → ∀ n : ℕ, c ≤ n →
        ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map
          (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
            (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := by
  classical
  induction i using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | h i ih =>
    by_cases hi1 : i = 1
    · subst i
      exact ⟨m, fun M hM n hmn ↦
        tor_one_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_smul_eq_bot I M m n hM hmn⟩
    · obtain ⟨cK, hcK⟩ := ih (i - 1) (by omega) (by omega)
      let Q : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ m)
      have : Module.Finite A (A ⧸ I ^ m) := Module.Finite.quotient A (I ^ m)
      obtain ⟨cF, hcF⟩ :=
        exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_finite I Q i (by omega)
      let c := max cK cF
      refine ⟨2 * c, fun M hM n hn ↦ ?_⟩
      have hc : c ≤ n := by dsimp [c] at *; omega
      have hcn : c ≤ n - c := by dsimp [c] at *; omega
      have hcK_n : cK ≤ n := (Nat.le_max_left cK cF).trans hc
      have hcF_nc : cF ≤ n - c := (Nat.le_max_right cK cF).trans hcn
      let : DecidableEq (M : Type u) := Classical.decEq M
      let F : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A ((M : Type u) →₀ A ⧸ I ^ m)
      let ε : F ⟶ M := ModuleCat.ofHom (boundedTorsionPresentationMap I m M hM)
      let K := LinearMap.ker ε.hom
      let S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
        ShortComplex.mk (ModuleCat.ofHom K.subtype) ε (by
          apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
          exact LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ x.2)
      have hFbound : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A F) = ⊥ := by
        simpa [F] using
          (pow_smul_finsupp_eq_bot (A := A) I m (ι := (M : Type u)))
      have hKbound : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A K) = ⊥ :=
        pow_smul_ker_eq_bot I m ε hFbound
      have hS : S.ShortExact := by
        refine ShortComplex.ShortExact.mk' ?_ ?_ ?_
        · rw [ShortComplex.ShortExact.moduleCat_exact_iff_function_exact]
          exact LinearMap.exact_subtype_ker_map ε.hom
        · rw [ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective]
          exact K.subtype_injective
        · rw [ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective]
          exact boundedTorsionPresentationMap_surjective I m M hM
      let q₀ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)
      let q₁ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - c))
      let q₂ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - 2 * c))
      have h₀₁ : n - c ≤ n := by omega
      have h₁₂ : n - 2 * c ≤ n - c := by omega
      have h₀₂ : n - 2 * c ≤ n := by omega
      let tr₀₁ : q₀ ⟶ q₁ := ModuleCat.ofHom
        (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁))
      let tr₁₂ : q₁ ⟶ q₂ := ModuleCat.ofHom
        (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ (n - c)) (p' := I ^ (n - 2 * c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₁₂))
      let tr₀₂ : q₀ ⟶ q₂ := ModuleCat.ofHom
        (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - 2 * c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₂))
      have htr : tr₀₁ ≫ tr₁₂ = tr₀₂ :=
        ModuleCat.hom_ext (Submodule.factor_comp (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁)
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₁₂))
      let ψ := torSESShortComplexTransition hS tr₀₁ i hi
      let θ := torSESShortComplexTransition hS tr₁₂ i hi
      have hψ : ψ.τ₃ = 0 := by
        show ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (i - 1)).obj (ModuleCat.of A K)).map tr₀₁ = 0
        apply tor_transition_zero_to_target I (ModuleCat.of A K)
          (i - 1) cK n (n - c) hcK_n (by omega)
        exact hcK (ModuleCat.of A K) hKbound n hcK_n
      have hθ : θ.τ₁ = 0 := by
        show ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj F).map tr₁₂ = 0
        have hQsmall := hcF (n - c) hcF_nc
        have hQlarge := tor_transition_zero_to_target I Q i cF (n - c) (n - 2 * c)
          hcF_nc (by omega) hQsmall
        apply tor_transition_zero_finsupp i Q q₁ q₂ tr₁₂
        exact hQlarge
      have hT : (torSESShortComplex hS q₁ i hi).Exact := torSES_exact hS q₁ i hi
      have hzero := shortComplex_twoStep_zero hT ψ θ hψ hθ
      have hmap : ψ.τ₂ ≫ θ.τ₂ = ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map tr₀₂ := by
        show ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map tr₀₁ ≫
            ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map tr₁₂ =
          ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map tr₀₂
        rw [← Functor.map_comp, htr]
      have hmain : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map tr₀₂ = 0 := by
        rw [← hmap]
        exact hzero
      simpa only [tr₀₂, q₀, q₂] using hmain

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0G9X.** For a fixed power `I ^ m` and a positive Tor degree, there is
a uniform shift such that the transition from `A / I ^ n` to `A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero
map on Tor against every module annihilated by `I ^ m`. -/
@[stacks 0G9X]
theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_smul_eq_bot
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A) (m i : ℕ) (hi : 0 < i) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A),
      I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥ → ∀ n : ℕ, c ≤ n →
        ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).map
          (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
            (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 :=
  exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_core I m i hi

/-! ### The connecting window of the long exact sequence in the first variable -/

/-- The connecting map of a short exact sequence of first variables, followed by the map induced
by its injection, is zero. -/
private theorem torDelta_comp_tor_map_eq_zero
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)) (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (k : ℕ) :
    torDelta S hS N k ≫ ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) k).map S.f).app N = 0 := by
  have hrel : (ComplexShape.down ℕ).Rel (k + 1) k := by simp [ComplexShape.down_Rel]
  have hδ : (lesShift.ses A S hS N).δ (k + 1) k hrel ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
        ((lesShift.phi A (projectiveResolution N).complex).map S.f) k = 0 :=
    (lesShift.ses A S hS N).δ_comp (k + 1) k hrel
  have h1 : torDelta S hS N k ≫ ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) k).map S.f).app N
      = (torIsoHomology S.X₃ N (k + 1)).hom ≫
        ((lesShift.ses A S hS N).δ (k + 1) k hrel ≫ HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
          ((lesShift.phi A (projectiveResolution N).complex).map S.f) k) ≫
        (torIsoHomology S.X₂ N k).inv := by
    rw [torDelta]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [← torIsoHomology_inv_naturality S.f N k]
  rw [h1, hδ, Limits.zero_comp, Limits.comp_zero]

/-- The window `Tor_{k+1}(S.X₃, N) → Tor_k(S.X₁, N) → Tor_k(S.X₂, N)` of the long exact sequence
attached to a short exact sequence `S` of first variables. -/
private noncomputable def torShortComplexDeltaFirst
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)) (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (k : ℕ) : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
  ShortComplex.mk (torDelta S hS N k) (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) k).map S.f).app N)
    (torDelta_comp_tor_map_eq_zero S hS N k)

/-- The window `Tor_{k+1}(S.X₃, N) → Tor_k(S.X₁, N) → Tor_k(S.X₂, N)` is exact. -/
private theorem torShortComplexDeltaFirst_exact
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)) (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (k : ℕ) : (torShortComplexDeltaFirst S hS N k).Exact := by
  have hrel : (ComplexShape.down ℕ).Rel (k + 1) k := by simp [ComplexShape.down_Rel]
  refine ShortComplex.exact_of_iso ?_ ((lesShift.ses A S hS N).homology_exact₁ (k + 1) k hrel)
  refine ShortComplex.isoMk (torIsoHomology S.X₃ N (k + 1)).symm
    (torIsoHomology S.X₁ N k).symm (torIsoHomology S.X₂ N k).symm ?_
    (torIsoHomology_inv_naturality S.f N k).symm
  show (torIsoHomology S.X₃ N (k + 1)).inv ≫ torDelta S hS N k
    = (lesShift.ses A S hS N).δ (k + 1) k hrel ≫ (torIsoHomology S.X₁ N k).inv
  rw [torDelta, Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

/-- A class in `Tor_k(S.X₁, N)` killed by the injection of `S` is the image of a class in
`Tor_{k+1}(S.X₃, N)` under the connecting map. -/
private theorem exists_torDelta_eq_of_tor_map_eq_zero
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)) (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (N : ModuleCat.{u} A) (k : ℕ)
    (w : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) k).obj S.X₁).obj N : Type u))
    (hw : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) k).map S.f).app N).hom w = 0) :
    ∃ y : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (k + 1)).obj S.X₃).obj N : Type u),
      (torDelta S hS N k).hom y = w :=
  (ShortComplex.moduleCat_exact_iff (torShortComplexDeltaFirst S hS N k)).mp
    (torShortComplexDeltaFirst_exact S hS N k) w hw

/-- The connecting map of a short exact sequence of first variables is natural in the second
variable. -/
private theorem torDelta_naturality_in_second
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {S : ShortComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A)} (hS : S.ShortExact)
    {N N' : ModuleCat.{u} A} (g : N ⟶ N') (k : ℕ) :
    (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (k + 1)).obj S.X₃).map g) ≫ torDelta S hS N' k =
      torDelta S hS N k ≫ (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) k).obj S.X₁).map g) :=
  torSESDelta_naturality_in_second hS g (k + 1) (Nat.succ_pos k)

/-! ### The sandwich step -/

/-- **The sandwich step.** Let `M` sit in two short exact sequences, as the middle term of
`0 → MK → M → ME → 0` and of `0 → ME → M → MQ → 0`, in such a way that the composite
`M → ME → M` induces the zero map on `Tor_j(-, N₀)`. If a map `w₁ : N₀ ⟶ N₁` of second variables
kills `Tor_{j+1}(MQ, -)` and a map `w₂ : N₁ ⟶ N₂` kills `Tor_j(MK, -)`, then the composite
`w₁ ≫ w₂` kills `Tor_j(M, -)`.

This is the diagram chase of [Stacks, Tag 0GA2]: a class of `Tor_j(M, N₀)` maps into
`Tor_j(ME, N₀)` inside the image of the connecting map of the second sequence, so it dies after
`w₁`; what remains comes from `Tor_j(MK, N₁)`, so it dies after `w₂`. -/
private theorem tor_map_comp_eq_zero_of_sandwich
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {MK M ME MQ N₀ N₁ N₂ : ModuleCat.{u} A}
    (ja : MK ⟶ M) (p : M ⟶ ME) (ι : ME ⟶ M) (pr : M ⟶ MQ)
    (z₁ : ja ≫ p = 0) (z₂ : ι ≫ pr = 0)
    (hS₁ : (ShortComplex.mk ja p z₁).ShortExact)
    (hS₂ : (ShortComplex.mk ι pr z₂).ShortExact)
    (j : ℕ) (w₁ : N₀ ⟶ N₁) (w₂ : N₁ ⟶ N₂)
    (hmul : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map (p ≫ ι)).app N₀ = 0)
    (hQ : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (j + 1)).obj MQ).map w₁ = 0)
    (hK : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj MK).map w₂ = 0) :
    ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map w₁ ≫ ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map w₂ = 0 := by
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  apply LinearMap.ext
  intro x
  -- The image of `x` in `Tor_j(ME, N₀)` is killed by the injection of the second sequence.
  have hcomp : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map p).app N₀ ≫ ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map ι).app N₀
      = ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map (p ≫ ι)).app N₀ := by
    rw [Functor.map_comp, NatTrans.comp_app]
  have hker : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map ι).app N₀).hom
      ((((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map p).app N₀).hom x) = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom x) (hcomp.trans hmul)
    simpa using h
  -- Hence it is the image of a class in `Tor_{j+1}(MQ, N₀)` under the connecting map.
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := exists_torDelta_eq_of_tor_map_eq_zero (ShortComplex.mk ι pr z₂) hS₂ N₀ j
    ((((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map p).app N₀).hom x) hker
  -- That class dies under `w₁`, so the image of `x` in `Tor_j(ME, N₁)` vanishes.
  have hδnat := torDelta_naturality_in_second hS₂ w₁ j
  have hME : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj ME).map w₁).hom
      ((((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map p).app N₀).hom x) = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom y) hδnat
    simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply] at h
    rw [hy] at h
    have hy0 : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (j + 1)).obj MQ).map w₁).hom y = 0 := by
      rw [hQ]; rfl
    rw [hy0] at h
    simp only [map_zero] at h
    exact h.symm
  -- The image of `x` under `w₁` is therefore killed by `p`.
  have hpnat := ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map p).naturality w₁
  have hx₁ : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map p).app N₁).hom
      ((((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map w₁).hom x) = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom x) hpnat
    simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply] at h
    rw [h]
    exact hME
  -- So it comes from `Tor_j(MK, N₁)`, which dies under `w₂`.
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := exists_tor_map_eq_of_tor_map_eq_zero (ShortComplex.mk ja p z₁) hS₁ N₁ j
    ((((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map w₁).hom x) hx₁
  have hjanat := ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map ja).naturality w₂
  have hfin : (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map w₂).hom
      ((((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map w₁).hom x) = 0 := by
    rw [← hz]
    have h := congrArg (fun f ↦ f.hom z) hjanat
    simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply] at h
    rw [← h, hK]
    simp
  simpa using hfin

/-! ### Stacks tag 0GA2 -/

/-- The descending induction of [Stacks, Tag 0GA2]. With `c₁` a uniform annihilator exponent for
`Tor_i^A(M, A/I^q)` in degrees `i > e`, write `v` for a set of indices `k` whose power
`g k ^ c₁` acts as zero on `M`. For each `d ≤ t` there are `N` and `c`, depending only on `A`,
`I`, `g`, `e`, `c₁` and `d`, such that the transition `A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the
zero map on `Tor_j^A(M, -)` for every `M` admitting such a `v` of size at least `t - d`, every
degree `j` with `e + 1 ≤ j ≤ e + 1 + (t - d)`, and every `n ≥ N`.

At `d = 0` the hypothesis forces every `g k ^ c₁` to kill `M`, hence a fixed power of `I` to
kill `M`, and the uniform vanishing for modules of bounded torsion applies. Each further step
replaces `M` by the kernel and the cokernel of multiplication by `g k ^ c₁` for an index `k`
outside `v`, both of which admit a larger `v`; the price is one degree, one more unit of `N` and
a doubling of `c`.

The level `e` of the annihilation hypothesis and the number `t` of generators play separate
roles: the induction runs over the generators, while the degree window is pinned to `e`. -/
private theorem uniform_tor_transition_descent
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ}
    (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) (e c₁ : ℕ)
    (hann : ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i q : ℕ), e < i →
      I ^ c₁ ≤ Module.annihilator A
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ q)))) :
    ∀ d : ℕ, d ≤ t → ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (v : Finset (Fin t)),
      t - d ≤ v.card → (∀ k ∈ v, ∀ x : (M : Type u), g k ^ c₁ • x = 0) →
      ∀ j : ℕ, e + 1 ≤ j → j ≤ e + 1 + (t - d) → ∀ n : ℕ, N ≤ n →
        ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj M).map
          (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
            (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := by
  classical
  intro d
  induction d with
  | zero =>
    intro _
    -- A power of `I` lies in the ideal generated by the `c₁`-st powers of the generators.
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ : ∃ m : ℕ, I ^ m ≤ Ideal.span (Set.range fun k : Fin t ↦ g k ^ c₁) := by
      refine Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg ?_ (IsNoetherian.noetherian I)
      rw [hg, Ideal.span_le]
      rintro y ⟨k, rfl⟩
      exact Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mpr ⟨c₁, Ideal.subset_span ⟨k, rfl⟩⟩
    have hex : ∀ j : ℕ, ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A),
        I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A M) = ⊥ → ∀ n : ℕ, c ≤ n →
          ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (j + 1)).obj M).map
            (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
              (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := fun j ↦
      exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_smul_eq_bot I m (j + 1) (Nat.succ_pos j)
    choose cf hcf using hex
    refine ⟨(Finset.range (e + t + 1)).sup cf, (Finset.range (e + t + 1)).sup cf, ?_⟩
    intro M v hv hvk j hj1 hj2 n hn
    -- The index set is everything, so every `g k ^ c₁` kills `M`.
    have hall : ∀ k : Fin t, ∀ x : (M : Type u), g k ^ c₁ • x = 0 := by
      intro k x
      refine hvk k ?_ x
      have hcard : v.card ≤ Fintype.card (Fin t) := Finset.card_le_univ v
      have huniv : v = Finset.univ := by
        refine Finset.eq_univ_of_card v ?_
        simp only [Fintype.card_fin] at hcard ⊢
        omega
      rw [huniv]
      exact Finset.mem_univ k
    have hJann : Ideal.span (Set.range fun k : Fin t ↦ g k ^ c₁)
        ≤ Module.annihilator A (M : Type u) := by
      rw [Ideal.span_le]
      rintro y ⟨k, rfl⟩
      exact Module.mem_annihilator.mpr fun x ↦ hall k x
    have hM : I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule A (M : Type u)) = ⊥ := by
      exact (ideal_smul_top_eq_bot_iff _).mpr fun a ha x ↦
        Module.mem_annihilator.mp (hJann (hm ha)) x
    obtain ⟨j', rfl⟩ : ∃ j' : ℕ, j = j' + 1 := ⟨j - 1, by omega⟩
    have hmem : j' ∈ Finset.range (e + t + 1) := Finset.mem_range.mpr (by omega)
    have hle : cf j' ≤ (Finset.range (e + t + 1)).sup cf := Finset.le_sup hmem
    exact tor_transition_zero_to_target I M (j' + 1) (cf j') n
      (n - (Finset.range (e + t + 1)).sup cf) (le_trans hle hn) (by omega)
      (hcf j' M hM n (le_trans hle hn))
  | succ d ih =>
    intro hdt
    obtain ⟨N, c, hH⟩ := ih (by omega)
    refine ⟨N + 2 * c, 2 * c, ?_⟩
    intro M v hv hvk j hj1 hj2 n hn
    have h₀₁ : n - c ≤ n := by omega
    have h₁₂ : n - 2 * c ≤ n - c := by omega
    have h₀₂ : n - 2 * c ≤ n := by omega
    by_cases hbig : t - d ≤ v.card
    · exact tor_transition_zero_to_target I M j c n (n - 2 * c) (by omega) (by omega)
        (hH M v hbig hvk j hj1 (by omega) n (by omega))
    -- The index set is proper, so some `g k ^ c₁` is not known to kill `M`.
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ : ∃ k : Fin t, k ∉ v := by
      by_contra hcon
      have hforall : ∀ k : Fin t, k ∈ v := fun k ↦ not_not.mp fun hkv ↦ hcon ⟨k, hkv⟩
      rw [Finset.eq_univ_iff_forall.mpr hforall] at hbig
      simp only [Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin] at hbig
      omega
    -- Multiplication by `g k ^ c₁`, its kernel, its image and the cokernel.
    set mulB : M ⟶ M := g k ^ c₁ • 𝟙 M with hmulB
    set Kb : Submodule A (M : Type u) := LinearMap.ker mulB.hom with hKb
    set Eb : Submodule A (M : Type u) := LinearMap.range mulB.hom with hEb
    have hmulBapp : ∀ x : (M : Type u), mulB.hom x = g k ^ c₁ • x := fun _ ↦ rfl
    let MK : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A Kb
    let MQ : ModuleCat.{u} A := ModuleCat.of A ((M : Type u) ⧸ Eb)
    let ja : MK ⟶ M := ModuleCat.ofHom Kb.subtype
    let pp : M ⟶ ModuleCat.of A Eb := ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.rangeRestrict mulB.hom)
    let ii : ModuleCat.of A Eb ⟶ M := ModuleCat.ofHom Eb.subtype
    let pr : M ⟶ MQ := ModuleCat.ofHom Eb.mkQ
    have z₁ : ja ≫ pp = 0 := by
      apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
      apply LinearMap.ext
      intro x
      exact Subtype.ext (LinearMap.mem_ker.mp x.2)
    have z₂ : ii ≫ pr = 0 := by
      apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
      apply LinearMap.ext
      intro x
      exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero Eb).mpr x.2
    have hS₁ : (ShortComplex.mk ja pp z₁).ShortExact := by
      refine ShortComplex.ShortExact.mk' ?_ ?_ ?_
      · rw [ShortComplex.ShortExact.moduleCat_exact_iff_function_exact]
        intro y
        constructor
        · intro hy
          exact ⟨⟨y, LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr (congrArg Subtype.val hy)⟩, rfl⟩
        · rintro ⟨z, rfl⟩
          exact Subtype.ext (LinearMap.mem_ker.mp z.2)
      · rw [ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective]
        exact Kb.subtype_injective
      · rw [ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective]
        exact LinearMap.surjective_rangeRestrict mulB.hom
    have hS₂ : (ShortComplex.mk ii pr z₂).ShortExact := by
      refine ShortComplex.ShortExact.mk' ?_ ?_ ?_
      · rw [ShortComplex.ShortExact.moduleCat_exact_iff_function_exact]
        intro y
        constructor
        · intro hy
          exact ⟨⟨y, (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero Eb).mp hy⟩, rfl⟩
        · rintro ⟨z, rfl⟩
          exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero Eb).mpr z.2
      · rw [ModuleCat.mono_iff_injective]
        exact Eb.subtype_injective
      · rw [ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective]
        exact Eb.mkQ_surjective
    have hfac : pp ≫ ii = mulB := by
      apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
      apply LinearMap.ext
      intro x
      rfl
    -- The composite `M → g k ^ c₁ · M → M` is zero on `Tor_j`, by the uniform annihilation.
    have hmul : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).map (pp ≫ ii)).app
        (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n)) = 0 := by
      have hgkI : g k ∈ I := by rw [hg]; exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨k, rfl⟩
      have hbI : g k ^ c₁ ∈ I ^ c₁ := Ideal.pow_mem_pow hgkI c₁
      rw [hfac, hmulB, tor_map_smul_id]
      apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
      apply LinearMap.ext
      intro y
      show g k ^ c₁ • y = 0
      exact Module.mem_annihilator.mp (hann M j n (by omega) hbI) y
    -- Both the kernel and the cokernel admit one more index.
    have hcardins : t - d ≤ (insert k v).card := by
      rw [Finset.card_insert_of_notMem hk]
      omega
    have hKv : ∀ k' ∈ insert k v, ∀ x : (MK : Type u), g k' ^ c₁ • x = 0 := by
      intro k' hk' x
      refine Subtype.ext ?_
      rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hk' with rfl | hk'v
      · exact LinearMap.mem_ker.mp x.2
      · exact hvk k' hk'v (x : (M : Type u))
    have hQv : ∀ k' ∈ insert k v, ∀ x : (MQ : Type u), g k' ^ c₁ • x = 0 := by
      intro k' hk' x
      obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective Eb x
      rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul]
      rcases Finset.mem_insert.mp hk' with rfl | hk'v
      · exact (Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero Eb).mpr ⟨y, rfl⟩
      · rw [hvk k' hk'v y]
        exact Submodule.Quotient.mk_zero Eb
    have hQ : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (j + 1)).obj MQ).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁))) = 0 :=
      hH MQ (insert k v) hcardins hQv (j + 1) (by omega) (by omega) n (by omega)
    have hK : ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj MK).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ (n - c)) (p' := I ^ (n - 2 * c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₁₂))) = 0 :=
      tor_transition_zero_to_target I MK j c (n - c) (n - 2 * c) (by omega) (by omega)
        (hH MK (insert k v) hcardins hKv j hj1 (by omega) (n - c) (by omega))
    have hu : (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁)) :
            ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ n) ⟶ ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ (n - c))) ≫
        ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ (n - c)) (p' := I ^ (n - 2 * c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₁₂))
        = ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - 2 * c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₂)) := by
      apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
      exact Submodule.factor_comp (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₀₁) (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right h₁₂)
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (tor_map_comp_eq_zero_of_sandwich ja pp ii pr z₁ z₂ hS₁ hS₂ j _ _
      hmul hQ hK)
    rw [← Functor.map_comp, hu]

/-- Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` generated by at most `t`
elements, and let `e` be a degree above which a single power `I ^ c₁`, depending on `A` and `I`
alone, annihilates `Tor_i^A(M, A/I^q)` for every `A`-module `M` and every `q`. There are `N` and
`c`, depending only on `A`, `I`, `t`, `e` and `c₁`, such that the surjection
`A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map
`Tor_{e+1}^A(M, A/I^n) → Tor_{e+1}^A(M, A/I^{n-c})` for *every* `A`-module `M` and every
`n ≥ N`.

The level `e` is arbitrary and in particular may be smaller than `t`: the descending induction
on the generators of `I` costs one degree per generator above the level, not a level. -/
theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ}
    (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) (e c₁ : ℕ)
    (hann : ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i q : ℕ), e < i →
      I ^ c₁ ≤ Module.annihilator A
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ q)))) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (n : ℕ), N ≤ n →
      ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (e + 1)).obj M).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨N, c, hH⟩ := uniform_tor_transition_descent g hg e c₁ hann t le_rfl
  exact ⟨N, c, fun M n hn ↦ hH M ∅ (by simp)
    (fun k hk ↦ absurd hk (Finset.notMem_empty k)) (e + 1) le_rfl (by omega) n hn⟩

/-- Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring `A` generated by at most `t`
elements. There are `N` and `c`, depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`, such that the surjection
`A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map
`Tor_{t+1}^A(M, A/I^n) → Tor_{t+1}^A(M, A/I^{n-c})` for *every* `A`-module `M` and every
`n ≥ N`; the two constants are chosen before the module is seen.

The hypothesis `hann` is the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0GA1], stated for the model of `Tor`
that derives the second variable: a single power `I ^ c₁`, depending on `A` and `I` alone,
annihilates `Tor_i^A(M, A/I^q)` for every `A`-module `M`, every degree `i > t` and every `q`. -/
theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ}
    (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) (c₁ : ℕ)
    (hann : ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i q : ℕ), t < i →
      I ^ c₁ ≤ Module.annihilator A
        (((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ q)))) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (n : ℕ), N ≤ n →
      ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (t + 1)).obj M).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 :=
  exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level g hg t c₁ hann

/-- The level form of [Stacks, Tag 0GA2], with the annihilation hypothesis written in the model
of `Tor` which derives the first variable, so that it is the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0GA1] at
level `e` verbatim. -/
theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level_tor'
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ}
    (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) (e c₁ : ℕ)
    (hann : ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (i q : ℕ), e < i →
      I ^ c₁ ≤ Module.annihilator A
        (((Tor' (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj M).obj (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I ^ q)))) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (n : ℕ), N ≤ n →
      ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (e + 1)).obj M).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := by
  refine exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level g hg e c₁ ?_
  intro M i q hi r hr
  exact mem_annihilator_of_moduleCat_iso (((Tor_iso_Tor' A i).app M).app _).symm
    (hann M i q hi hr)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0GA2.** Let `I = (g 0, …, g (t - 1))` be an ideal of a Noetherian ring
`A` generated by at most `t` elements. There are `N` and `c`, depending only on `A`, `I` and `t`,
such that the surjection `A / I ^ n ↠ A / I ^ (n - c)` induces the zero map
`Tor_{t+1}^A(M, A/I^n) → Tor_{t+1}^A(M, A/I^{n-c})` for *every* `A`-module `M` and every
`n ≥ N`. That `N` and `c` are produced before the module is seen is the whole content of the
source's lemma.

The power `I ^ c₁` annihilating `Tor_i^A(M, A/I^q)` for all `M`, all `i > t` and all `q`, which
the source's induction starts from, is [Stacks, Tag 0GA1],
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII.exists_pow_le_annihilator_tor_quotient_pow_blowup`. -/
@[stacks 0GA2]
theorem exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_tor'
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A} {t : ℕ}
    (g : Fin t → A) (hg : I = Ideal.span (Set.range g)) :
    ∃ N c : ℕ, ∀ (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (n : ℕ), N ≤ n →
      ((Tor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (t + 1)).obj M).map
        (ModuleCat.ofHom (Submodule.factor (p := I ^ n) (p' := I ^ (n - c))
          (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)))) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨c₁, hann⟩ :=
    Stacks.LocalCohomology.UniformityII.exists_pow_le_annihilator_tor_quotient_pow_blowup g hg
  exact exists_uniform_tor_transition_eq_zero_of_pow_le_annihilator_level_tor' g hg t c₁ hann
